{
  "title": "Stage 2: An intermediate with a path length",
  "summary": "Sign an intermediate CA with your root and limit what it may issue.",
  "minutes": 15,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Briefing: why an intermediate",
      "body": [
        "Real roots live offline. Day-to-day issuing is done by an **intermediate** that the root signs once. If the intermediate leaks, you revoke it and sign a new one; the root, and every client that trusts it, stays put.",
        "",
        "Add `intermediate NAME`. It is signed by the **most recent root**, valid **2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01**, and has Basic Constraints **CA with path length 0**: it may sign leaves but not further CAs. This is `basicConstraints = critical, CA:TRUE, pathlen:0` in an openssl extfile.",
        "",
        "`show` now prints the path length, and `list` says who issued what:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "> root Dojo Root",
        "> intermediate Issuing CA",
        "> show Issuing CA",
        "> list",
        "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
        "created intermediate CN=Issuing CA under CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)",
        "CN=Issuing CA",
        "  issuer: CN=Dojo Root",
        "  ca: yes, pathlen 0",
        "  valid: 2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01",
        "root CN=Dojo Root",
        "intermediate CN=Issuing CA (issued by CN=Dojo Root)",
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blanks",
      "prompt": "Complete the intermediate's Basic Constraints: a CA, **with** a path length constraint of 0, critical.",
      "code": [
        "new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(__1__, __2__, __3__, __4__)"
      ],
      "blanks": [
        "true",
        "true",
        "0",
        "true"
      ],
      "bank": [
        "false",
        "1",
        "-1"
      ],
      "explain": "Arguments: certificateAuthority, hasPathLengthConstraint, pathLengthConstraint, critical. The root uses `(true, false, 0, true)`: no limit."
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "A root has no path length limit; its intermediate has `pathlen:0`. The intermediate signs another CA certificate, `CN=Rogue CA`, which then signs a leaf. What does a validator do with that leaf?",
      "options": [
        "Rejects the chain: a CA below a pathlen:0 intermediate is not allowed",
        "Accepts it, because the root has no limit",
        "Accepts it only if Rogue CA also has pathlen:0",
        "Rejects only the Rogue CA certificate but trusts the leaf"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "Path length counts the CA certificates that may follow. `pathlen:0` means none: only end-entity certificates may sit below it."
    },
    {
      "type": "order",
      "prompt": "Put the lines of `MakeIntermediate` in order.",
      "lines": [
        "var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "var req = new CertificateRequest(\"CN=\" + name, key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(true, true, 0, true));",
        "using var pub = req.Create(parent.Cert, Day(2030), Day(2040), Serial());",
        "return new Entry(name, \"intermediate\", pub.CopyWithPrivateKey(key), parent);"
      ],
      "explain": "Extensions go in before signing. `Create` returns a certificate without a private key; the intermediate needs its key to sign leaves in stage 3, so attach it."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "Your `show` reads Basic Constraints back. For the intermediate, what are `bc.CertificateAuthority`, `bc.HasPathLengthConstraint` and `bc.PathLengthConstraint`? Type them comma-separated, like `True, False, 3`.",
      "code": [
        "var bc = inter.Extensions.OfType<X509BasicConstraintsExtension>().Single();",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"{bc.CertificateAuthority}, {bc.HasPathLengthConstraint}, {bc.PathLengthConstraint}\");"
      ],
      "answer": "True, True, 0",
      "verify": false,
      "explain": "That is what `new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(true, true, 0, true)` put in.",
      "accept": [
        "True,True,0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "mode": "write",
      "title": "mini-ca: intermediates",
      "prompt": [
        "Extend mini-ca.",
        "",
        "| Input | Prints |",
        "|---|---|",
        "| `intermediate NAME` | `created intermediate CN=NAME under CN=ROOT (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)` |",
        "",
        "- Signed by the most recently created root. With no root yet: `error: no root yet`. No name: `error: intermediate needs a name`. Existing name: `error: 'NAME' already exists`.",
        "- New P-256 key; Basic Constraints CA, path length 0, critical; Key Usage `KeyCertSign | CrlSign`, critical; SKI; AKI from the root; a serial unique per issuer (a counter is fine); returned **with** its private key.",
        "- `show`'s `ca:` line becomes `ca: no`, `ca: yes, pathlen N`, or `ca: yes, no pathlen limit`.",
        "- `list` adds ` (issued by ISSUER)` for certificates that have a parent.",
        "",
        "```text",
        "> root Dojo Root",
        "> intermediate Issuing CA",
        "> show Issuing CA",
        "> list",
        "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
        "created intermediate CN=Issuing CA under CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)",
        "CN=Issuing CA",
        "  issuer: CN=Dojo Root",
        "  ca: yes, pathlen 0",
        "  valid: 2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01",
        "root CN=Dojo Root",
        "intermediate CN=Issuing CA (issued by CN=Dojo Root)",
        "```",
        "",
        "Everything from stage 1 must keep working."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "using System.Security.Cryptography;",
        "using System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates;",
        "",
        "var certs = new Dictionary<string, Entry>();",
        "var order = new List<string>();",
        "int serials = 0;",
        "",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) != null)",
        "{",
        "    line = line.Trim();",
        "    if (line.Length == 0 || line.StartsWith(\"#\")) continue;",
        "    int space = line.IndexOf(' ');",
        "    string cmd = space < 0 ? line : line[..space];",
        "    string arg = space < 0 ? \"\" : line[(space + 1)..].Trim();",
        "    switch (cmd)",
        "    {",
        "        case \"root\":",
        "        {",
        "            if (arg == \"\") { Console.WriteLine(\"error: root needs a name\"); break; }",
        "            if (certs.ContainsKey(arg)) { Console.WriteLine($\"error: '{arg}' already exists\"); break; }",
        "           var made = Add(MakeRoot(arg));",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"created root {made.Cert.Subject} ({Dates(made.Cert)})\");",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "        case \"show\":",
        "        {",
        "            var found = Find(arg);",
        "            if (found != null) Show(found);",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "        case \"list\":",
        "        {",
        "            foreach (var name in order)",
        "            {",
        "                var x = certs[name];",
        "                Console.WriteLine(x.Parent == null ? $\"{x.Kind} {x.Cert.Subject}\" : $\"{x.Kind} {x.Cert.Subject} (issued by {x.Parent.Cert.Subject})\");",
        "            }",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "        default:",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"error: unknown command '{cmd}'\");",
        "            break;",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "Entry Add(Entry entry)",
        "{",
        "    certs[entry.Name] = entry;",
        "    order.Add(entry.Name);",
        "    return entry;",
        "}",
        "",
        "Entry? Find(string name)",
        "{",
        "    if (certs.TryGetValue(name, out var found)) return found;",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"error: no certificate named '{name}'\");",
        "    return null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "byte[] Serial() => new byte[] { 0x01, (byte)++serials };",
        "",
        "Entry MakeRoot(string name)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(\"CN=\" + name, key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(true, false, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(X509KeyUsageFlags.KeyCertSign | X509KeyUsageFlags.CrlSign, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    return new Entry(name, \"root\", req.CreateSelfSigned(Day(2030), Day(2050)), null);",
        "}",
        "",
        "void Show(Entry entry)",
        "{",
        "    var c = entry.Cert;",
        "    Console.WriteLine(c.Subject);",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"  issuer: {c.Issuer}\");",
        "    var bc = c.Extensions.OfType<X509BasicConstraintsExtension>().FirstOrDefault();",
        "   Console.WriteLine($\"  ca: {(bc != null && bc.CertificateAuthority ? \"yes\" : \"no\")}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"  valid: {Dates(c)}\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "static DateTimeOffset Day(int year) => new DateTimeOffset(year, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero);",
        "static string Ymd(DateTime t) => t.ToUniversalTime().ToString(\"yyyy-MM-dd\");",
        "static string Dates(X509Certificate2 c) => $\"{Ymd(c.NotBefore)} to {Ymd(c.NotAfter)}\";",
        "",
        "record Entry(string Name, string Kind, X509Certificate2 Cert, Entry? Parent);"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "using System.Security.Cryptography;",
        "using System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates;",
        "",
        "var certs = new Dictionary<string, Entry>();",
        "var order = new List<string>();",
        "int serials = 0;",
        "Entry? currentRoot = null;",
        "",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) != null)",
        "{",
        "    line = line.Trim();",
        "    if (line.Length == 0 || line.StartsWith(\"#\")) continue;",
        "    int space = line.IndexOf(' ');",
        "    string cmd = space < 0 ? line : line[..space];",
        "    string arg = space < 0 ? \"\" : line[(space + 1)..].Trim();",
        "    switch (cmd)",
        "    {",
        "        case \"root\":",
        "        {",
        "            if (arg == \"\") { Console.WriteLine(\"error: root needs a name\"); break; }",
        "            if (certs.ContainsKey(arg)) { Console.WriteLine($\"error: '{arg}' already exists\"); break; }",
        "           var made = currentRoot = Add(MakeRoot(arg));",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"created root {made.Cert.Subject} ({Dates(made.Cert)})\");",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "       case \"intermediate\":",
        "       {",
        "           if (arg == \"\") { Console.WriteLine(\"error: intermediate needs a name\"); break; }",
        "           if (certs.ContainsKey(arg)) { Console.WriteLine($\"error: '{arg}' already exists\"); break; }",
        "           if (currentRoot == null) { Console.WriteLine(\"error: no root yet\"); break; }",
        "           var made = Add(MakeIntermediate(arg, currentRoot));",
        "           Console.WriteLine($\"created intermediate {made.Cert.Subject} under {currentRoot.Cert.Subject} ({Dates(made.Cert)})\");",
        "           break;",
        "       }",
        "        case \"show\":",
        "        {",
        "            var found = Find(arg);",
        "            if (found != null) Show(found);",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "        case \"list\":",
        "        {",
        "            foreach (var name in order)",
        "            {",
        "                var x = certs[name];",
        "                Console.WriteLine(x.Parent == null ? $\"{x.Kind} {x.Cert.Subject}\" : $\"{x.Kind} {x.Cert.Subject} (issued by {x.Parent.Cert.Subject})\");",
        "            }",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "        default:",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"error: unknown command '{cmd}'\");",
        "            break;",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "Entry Add(Entry entry)",
        "{",
        "    certs[entry.Name] = entry;",
        "    order.Add(entry.Name);",
        "    return entry;",
        "}",
        "",
        "Entry? Find(string name)",
        "{",
        "    if (certs.TryGetValue(name, out var found)) return found;",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"error: no certificate named '{name}'\");",
        "    return null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "byte[] Serial() => new byte[] { 0x01, (byte)++serials };",
        "",
        "Entry MakeRoot(string name)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(\"CN=\" + name, key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(true, false, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(X509KeyUsageFlags.KeyCertSign | X509KeyUsageFlags.CrlSign, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    return new Entry(name, \"root\", req.CreateSelfSigned(Day(2030), Day(2050)), null);",
        "}",
        "",
        "Entry MakeIntermediate(string name, Entry parent)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(\"CN=\" + name, key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(true, true, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(X509KeyUsageFlags.KeyCertSign | X509KeyUsageFlags.CrlSign, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(X509AuthorityKeyIdentifierExtension.CreateFromCertificate(parent.Cert, true, false));",
        "    using var pub = req.Create(parent.Cert, Day(2030), Day(2040), Serial());",
        "    return new Entry(name, \"intermediate\", pub.CopyWithPrivateKey(key), parent);",
        "}",
        "",
        "void Show(Entry entry)",
        "{",
        "    var c = entry.Cert;",
        "    Console.WriteLine(c.Subject);",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"  issuer: {c.Issuer}\");",
        "    var bc = c.Extensions.OfType<X509BasicConstraintsExtension>().FirstOrDefault();",
        "   string ca = bc == null || !bc.CertificateAuthority ? \"no\"",
        "       : bc.HasPathLengthConstraint ? $\"yes, pathlen {bc.PathLengthConstraint}\" : \"yes, no pathlen limit\";",
        "   Console.WriteLine($\"  ca: {ca}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"  valid: {Dates(c)}\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "static DateTimeOffset Day(int year) => new DateTimeOffset(year, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero);",
        "static string Ymd(DateTime t) => t.ToUniversalTime().ToString(\"yyyy-MM-dd\");",
        "static string Dates(X509Certificate2 c) => $\"{Ymd(c.NotBefore)} to {Ymd(c.NotAfter)}\";",
        "",
        "record Entry(string Name, string Kind, X509Certificate2 Cert, Entry? Parent);"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Keep an `Entry? currentRoot` and set it in the `root` case.",
        "`X509AuthorityKeyIdentifierExtension.CreateFromCertificate(parent.Cert, true, false)` links the intermediate to its root.",
        "Serial: `byte[] Serial() => new byte[] { 0x01, (byte)++serials };` with `int serials = 0;` at the top."
      ],
      "carry": true,
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "issues an intermediate under the root",
          "stdin": [
            "root Dojo Root",
            "intermediate Issuing CA",
            "show Issuing CA",
            "show Dojo Root"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
            "created intermediate CN=Issuing CA under CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)",
            "CN=Issuing CA",
            "  issuer: CN=Dojo Root",
            "  ca: yes, pathlen 0",
            "  valid: 2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01",
            "CN=Dojo Root",
            "  issuer: CN=Dojo Root",
            "  ca: yes, no pathlen limit",
            "  valid: 2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "needs a root first",
          "stdin": [
            "intermediate Issuing CA",
            "root Dojo Root",
            "intermediate Issuing CA",
            "list"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "error: no root yet",
            "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
            "created intermediate CN=Issuing CA under CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)",
            "root CN=Dojo Root",
            "intermediate CN=Issuing CA (issued by CN=Dojo Root)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "signs with the most recent root",
          "stdin": [
            "root Old Root",
            "root New Root",
            "intermediate Issuing CA",
            "list"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "created root CN=Old Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
            "created root CN=New Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
            "created intermediate CN=Issuing CA under CN=New Root (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)",
            "root CN=Old Root",
            "root CN=New Root",
            "intermediate CN=Issuing CA (issued by CN=New Root)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "stage 1 still works",
          "stdin": [
            "root",
            "fly away",
            "root Dojo Root",
            "show Dojo Root"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "error: root needs a name",
            "error: unknown command 'fly'",
            "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
            "CN=Dojo Root",
            "  issuer: CN=Dojo Root",
            "  ca: yes, no pathlen limit",
            "  valid: 2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "still passes: creates a root and shows it",
          "stdin": [
            "root Dojo Root",
            "show Dojo Root"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
            "CN=Dojo Root",
            "  issuer: CN=Dojo Root",
            "  ca: yes, no pathlen limit",
            "  valid: 2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
